 "response": "Getosti's budget is now **$1,719K**.\n\n**Method**\n1. Only Finance Office budget lines count (set, increase, decrease). Messages from other teams and other Finance Office notices are ignored.\n2. For each withdrawal chain, I started from the last withdrawal and worked back to decide whether the original update stands.\n   - Example where the update stands: #0161 withdraws #0081, which withdrew #0032. So #0032 stands and withdraws #0015, which withdrew #0009. So #0009 stands and withdraws #0007, which means #0002 (+$472K) stands.\n   - Example where the update is cancelled: #1164 withdraws #0154, which withdrew #0021. So #0021 stands and withdraws #0013, which withdrew #0012. So #0012 stands, and #0003 (+$547K) is cancelled.\n3. Updates that end up cancelled include #0003, #0006, #0020, #0022, #0029, #0033, #0036, #0206, #0384, #0533, #0568 and #0339, along with roughly 90 others that were withdrawn directly.\n4. Updates whose withdrawal was itself undone, so they still apply, include #0002, #0028, #0051, #0052, #0071, #0093, #0201, #0236, #0275, #0414 and #0431.\n5. I then applied every remaining update in record order, starting from the $1,730K set in #0001. The total ends at $1,719K after the last update, #1590 (\u2212$25K).\n\nThis is a long hand calculation, so a small arithmetic slip somewhere in the chain is possible.\n\nANSWER: $1719K",
